## Exact cylinder validation failures

Non-invasive inspection of the exact packaged runtime's in-memory `SurfaceFinalValidationReport` identifies exactly three failed scalar thresholds:

1. `normalP95Degrees = 16.6272734366` > `15.0`;
2. `fieldP95Degrees = 37.9670987281` > `15.0`;
3. `warpageP95Degrees = 30.6213792811` > `30.0`.

All represented discrete strict/source-authoritative topology, boundary, feature-rail, provenance, local-sheet, degeneracy, manifold, inversion, self-intersection, convexity, valence, Euler, and component checks are green. Validation remains unchanged and authoritative.

The source-strip correction improved geometric source coverage substantially, including source-to-output P95 `0.104464 -> 0.008174`, but field P95 remained exactly `37.9671°` and warpage moved marginally over threshold.

## Root structural blocker

Adjacent canonical annulus rings admit two source-topologically valid one-to-one correspondences because each triangulated strip contains both same-column axial edges and diagonal inter-ring edges. Current production source sorts valid candidate vertex sequences lexicographically and selects `valid.front()`.

On the committed cylinder this chooses the diagonal/sheared correspondence. The selected inter-ring edge is **37.9670987281°** away from the axial cross-field family, exactly matching the failed field P95. This is a general field-authority ambiguity, not a fixture-count defect.

## Required next turn

Execute `.agents/Directional/Gate_3_Periodic_Ring_Correspondence_Code_Build_Plan.md` as **Code + Build only**.

The bounded correction must replace incidental lexicographic ring correspondence with an exact reciprocal cross-field-family-consistent correspondence while preserving annulus applicability, cut, holonomy, source-strip breakpoints, periodic quotient, provenance, and one-cell-to-one-quad materialization. Zero or genuinely ambiguous field-authoritative candidates must fail closed with typed periodic authority.

Do not relax validators, choose candidates by source ID/count/order/frequency, add fixture-specific logic, reintroduce fallback/recovery, use Euclidean seam welding, or broaden into G4/later work.

